enough, but go ahead and take it!

258
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:41,170
Ah!

259
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:42,570
Whooo!

260
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:47,376
Hey, I think I saw one of
them roll behind the bricks.

261
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:50,697
They're just coins, but
there are a lot of them.

262
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:51,610
Nice.

263
00:14:51,693 --> 00:14:53,300
Must be at least 20 pounds.

264
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,597
Hey, man, watch your feet.

265
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:55,510
You're steppin' on one.

266
00:14:55,593 --> 00:14:56,423
What's that?

267
00:14:56,506 --> 00:14:57,336
Ah!

268
00:14:57,419 --> 00:14:58,457
Pick up the damn coins later!

269
00:14:58,540 --> 00:15:00,137
You can have them all, okay?

270
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:01,720
Here you go, boys.

271
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,628
It's getting close to noon.

272
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:07,700
I made you boys some tea, so take
a load off and have some lunch.

273
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,620
Oh, sounds good to me.

274
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:12,640
Listen, Granny, I found
them first, so get lost!

275
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,567
Thank you very much, ma 'am.

276
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:17,500
Put them down!

277
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:19,737
I told you to hurry up and open the pipe!

278
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:21,996
If you don't, I'll crack your skulls!

279
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:29,920
It's open!

280
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:31,140
Move it!

281
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:35,900
Now die, Jotaro!

282
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,060
I won!

283
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:44,297
Just like the predictions said, I shot
the cocky bastard at the stroke of noon!

284
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:45,400
Go get him!

285
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:55,460
Old man, time to get up.

286
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:02,169
I don't think there's
any permanent damage.

287
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:04,920
I only have cuts and bruises.

288
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:07,840
But Polnareff, on the other hand...

289
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:11,897
Hey, don't mean to be a nuisance, but...

290
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:14,568
Could someone get this
damn thing off of me?

291
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:19,840
I won!

292
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:21,867
This is really gonna happen!

293
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:24,296
Tojoro's right in front of that pipe!

294
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:35,760
Huh? Ah, shoot!

295
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:42,130
What?!

296
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,230
Watch it.

297
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:49,051
Sorry about that, Jotaro.

298
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:51,337
I don't know what Whole
Horse was thinking,

299
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,277
but he decided sticking
his fingers on my nose

300
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:55,357
would be the perfect way
to spend the evening.

301
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:57,360
That guy is très disgusting.

302
00:16:57,900 --> 00:16:59,520
And my nose still itches.

303
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:01,180
So sorry again.

304
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:03,520
But how's it possible?

305
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:05,800
My bullet's missed!

306
00:17:07,580 --> 00:17:09,320
What the hell?

307
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:11,737
Were you trying to pull one over on me?

308
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:13,837
What the hell is going on around here?

309
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,560
I have no idea, yes.

310
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:19,800
Like I said, my predictions
always come true. It's fate.

311
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:21,120
I can't believe it.

312
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:25,577
Not once since I started using my stand
have my predictions ever been wrong.

313
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:29,157
Well, clearly there's a first time for
everything because they're still alive.

314
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:31,057
Not a single bullet hit his mark.

315
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:34,140
It's safe to say your
prediction was totally wrong.

316
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:35,310
Damn you.

317
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:38,777
Thanks for joining us
for today's broadcast.

318
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,297
Be sure to tune in next time.

319
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:42,086
Now for the 12 o 'clock news.

320
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:44,750
Huh?

321
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:48,580
What the hell?

322
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:52,089
There's no way in hell
it's just now, Noon.

323
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:54,880
I know what happened.

324
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,460
My watch is...

325
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:00,480
My watch is fast.

326
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:05,360
And that means I ended up firing
off the bullets before it was time.

327
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:06,960
But now it is, Noon.

328
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:08,777
What's that mean for us, huh?

329
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:13,520
Tell me, what the hell's going to happen
to us now that we've gone off script?

330
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:16,660
No, it can't be.

331
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:23,997
But where do we get off track?

332
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,597
It said the bullets will go right through

333
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,037
Joe Tarot's forehead
at the stroke of noon.

334
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:29,517
Hall Horse, the bullets are...

335
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,430
Come on!

336
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:33,501
All I need to know is
what's going to happen next!

337
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:48,239
Hey, tell me I'm not the only one
who heard that ear-piercing scream.

338
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:52,097
I'm not clear on the details, but
there's something fishy going on here.

339
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:54,237
But the bigger concern is this truck.

340
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:57,557
I think we'd better get out of here
before the cops start showing up.

341
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:58,581
Let's move, man.

342
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:03,240
But before we go, I want to know where
Whole Horse ran off to. I don't know.

343
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:05,284
He disappeared for some reason.

344
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:15,717
Hey, if you don't get away from that
pipe, you're going to get soaking wet.

345
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,800
You should try to be more careful.

346
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:25,340
Is he dead?

347
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:27,160
No, but he's critical.

348
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:31,708
I couldn't even begin to tell
you what transpired here today.

349
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:34,337
They looked him over and it
seems as though the bullet

350
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:36,717
went through his forehead
and out the top of his head.

351
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,797
One centimeter lower, and
he would have been a goner.

352
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:40,710
Oof.

353
00:19:40,793 --> 00:19:43,120
Gotta say, that is one lucky man.

354
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:50,500
In the end, it seems my
prediction was right.

355
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:54,780
Which means this was Whole
Horse's fate all along.

356
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,780
Jojo is really something else.

357
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:00,160
How lucky can one person be?

358
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:03,937
Both my brother and Whole
Horse were defeated by fate.

359
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:07,120
At this point, we stand
users are wasting our time.

360
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:09,967
Master Dios, the only
one who can defeat him.

361
00:20:11,860 --> 00:20:13,400
You know what, Zenyatta?

362
00:20:13,940 --> 00:20:16,540
Whole Horse, that big buffoon of a man,

363
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:20,271
taught me that revenge is
nothing more than a massive joke.

364
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:23,240
So, I'm going to forget about Jotaro.

365
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:25,600
I have a new path in life.

366
00:20:25,820 --> 00:20:29,440
I'll use my stand's powers to
help as many people as I can.

367
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:32,347
I'll use them to bring
happiness to everyone.

368
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:35,079
Maybe people will start to like us.

369
00:20:35,180 --> 00:20:37,709
And just maybe our
future will be brighter.

370
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:44,460
I'm tired of being afraid.

371
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:48,237
Today's the last day I spend under
a box cowering from everyone.

372
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,217
I learned a lot from this battle.

373
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:51,857
More than I thought I could.

374
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,646
I'm coming home now, brother.

375
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,440
I'm coming home to ask one to join you.

376
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,070
Huh? Huh?

377
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:02,440
Oh my gosh, I am so sorry.

378
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:04,266
I kicked it without thinking.

379
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,117
I didn't mean to hit you.

380
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:08,580
Please forgive me. Hold on.

381
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:11,220
This dog, he looks familiar.

382
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:13,716
I'm pretty sure I've seen him before.

383
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:14,960
But where?

384
00:21:16,540 --> 00:21:17,370
Ah!

385
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:18,860
There's no way!

386
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,160
It can't be!

387
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:22,070
No!

388
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:29,997
Hey, now that I think about
it, where'd our dumbass dog go?

389
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,477
You're talking about Iggy?

390
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:34,217
I'm sure he's scrounging
around for food somewhere.

391
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:38,097
I've said from the beginning he
wouldn't help us when we needed him.

392
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:40,877
He should have known it
wouldn't be so simple.

393
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:44,548
If people could change that
easily, life wouldn't be so hard.

394
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:49,237
So as fate would have it, Mondatta
joined Whole Horse in the hospital.

395
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:52,460
Only now, he was meager than ever before.

396
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,320
But, um...

397
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:59,400
Do you believe it?

398
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:01,180
I believe it!

399
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:04,340
Hell Horse! Bang! Compa!

400
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:07,421
I'm the player of the Hall Horse.

401
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:14,397
The card's name is Emperor.

402
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,760
Oh, I'm going to be a bong.

403
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:19,693
I'm going to be a fool.

404
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:23,300
But you're alright?

405
00:22:25,340 --> 00:22:26,600
I'm a bong.

406
00:22:27,140 --> 00:22:27,970
I'm a bong.

407
00:22:28,053 --> 00:22:30,277
I'm a bong. I'm a bong.

408
00:22:30,360 --> 00:22:31,540
I'm a bong.

409
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:33,080
I'm a bong.

410
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:40,397
I'm a bong.

411
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:44,357
I'm going to be 100 % of the manga.

412
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:47,400
So, this is how it's going.

413
00:22:48,020 --> 00:23:05,975
You can't believe it.

414
00:23:06,540 --> 00:23:07,658
You can believe it.

415
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:10,460
Hot horse! Boingo! Combi!

416
00:23:11,320 --> 00:23:12,150
I believe!

417
00:23:12,780 --> 00:23:14,300
Yes! Ok! I believe!

418
00:23:14,900 --> 00:23:16,280
Hot horse! Boingo!

419
00:23:17,180 --> 00:23:18,010
Combi!

420
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,960
The truth is,

421
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:22,313
I can't read correctly!

422
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:38,240
Good grief.

423
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:40,875
I have a soft spot for kid dog lovers.
